From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mozbuild: use ast.Constant instead of the removed ast.Str

Python 3.12 removed ast.Str, deprecated since 3.8 in favour of ast.Constant.
mozbuild's moz.build reader still builds one, so on a host Python of 3.12 or
newer configure dies before it has read a single build file:

  AttributeError: module 'ast' has no attribute 'Str'
  ==============================
  FATAL ERROR PROCESSING MOZBUILD FILE
  ==============================
      build/templates.mozbuild
  The error was triggered on line 8 of this file:
      @template

RewriteName.visit_Name rewrites every uppercase name in a moz.build file into
a subscript of the sandbox dict, and the subscript's slice was an
ast.Index(ast.Str(...)). ast.Constant is the spelling for both: it has been
the only string node since 3.8, and since 3.9 a subscript's slice is the
expression itself rather than an ast.Index wrapper - which is why the plain
ast.Constant below needs no Index around it. (ast.Index survives as a
deprecated no-op, so it is only the ast.Str that actually breaks.)

find_variables_from_ast had already been taught the 3.9 subscript form, but
kept an else branch for older Pythons that reaches for both removed names, and
its assigned_values helper was never converted at all. Since the tree cannot
be read by a Python that lacks ast.Constant, drop the dead branch rather than
extend the version test, and read .value where it read .s.

Upstream keeps ESR 128 on the Python versions that shipped with it, so this is
not fixed there; the same change landed on later trains.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/reader.py
+++ b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/reader.py
@@ -470,7 +470,7 @@
             return c(
                 ast.Subscript(
                     value=c(ast.Name(id=self._global_name, ctx=ast.Load())),
-                    slice=c(ast.Index(value=c(ast.Str(s=node.id)))),
+                    slice=c(ast.Constant(value=node.id)),
                     ctx=node.ctx,
                 )
             )
@@ -1027,16 +1027,9 @@
 
             key = None
             if isinstance(target, ast.Subscript):
-                # We need to branch to deal with python version differences.
-                if isinstance(target.slice, ast.Constant):
-                    # Python >= 3.9
-                    assert isinstance(target.slice.value, str)
-                    key = target.slice.value
-                else:
-                    # Others
-                    assert isinstance(target.slice, ast.Index)
-                    assert isinstance(target.slice.value, ast.Str)
-                    key = target.slice.value.s
+                assert isinstance(target.slice, ast.Constant)
+                assert isinstance(target.slice.value, str)
+                key = target.slice.value
 
             return name, key
 
@@ -1044,11 +1037,11 @@
             value = node.value
             if isinstance(value, ast.List):
                 for v in value.elts:
-                    assert isinstance(v, ast.Str)
-                    yield v.s
+                    assert isinstance(v, ast.Constant)
+                    yield v.value
             else:
-                assert isinstance(value, ast.Str)
-                yield value.s
+                assert isinstance(value, ast.Constant)
+                yield value.value
 
         assignments = []
 
